# Trivy ignore allowlist for bigcapital-fork.
#
# Policy:
#   1. Empty by default. The Trivy gate in .github/workflows/deploy.yml is
#      HIGH/CRITICAL only; medium/low findings flow into the report but
#      do not block deploys.
#   2. Add a CVE id (one per line, comment above with the why + an expiry
#      date) ONLY when:
#        - the CVE is in a transitive dep we can't bump, AND
#        - the affected code path is unreachable in our deployment, AND
#        - upstream has acknowledged the issue with no patched version yet.
#   3. Revisit every entry quarterly; remove the line once the dep is
#      upgraded past the affected version.
#
# Do NOT add entries to silence noise without root-cause analysis. The
# server Dockerfile already strips npm from the runtime to remove the
# noisiest source of HIGH CVEs.
